{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And I</b> — as its plain sense." "<b>Poor and needy</b> — either as a poor and needy one, or according to the enemies' thinking, and not like: \"they say of me, 'He is my brother.'\"" "<b>Do not delay</b> — my help is a transitive verb, or an intransitive verb." "<b>Do not delay</b> — like \"why do you delay,\" since You are my help."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 70, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:47.112266810Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}